# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This repo lives in a OneDrive folder and is edited from both macOS and
# Windows machines. Without this, a file saved on Windows syncs back with CRLF
# endings and shows up as an entire-file diff (every line deleted and re-added)
# that hides any real change underneath. `eol=lf` — not just `text=auto` — is
# what keeps the checkout itself LF on Windows, so the round trip is a no-op.
#
# The shell scripts additionally *require* LF: bash chokes on `\r` in build
# scripts, so CRLF there would break scripts/build-*.sh outright.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these. Git's auto-detection already classifies
# them correctly, but naming them explicitly means a stray edit or a new
# detection heuristic can't corrupt an icon or a screenshot by "fixing"
# byte sequences that merely look like line endings.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
